    "updated_at": "2024-07-29T17:52:37Z",
    "body": "I don't have any strong objection to an explicit option to turn on the behavior of always settling the previous promise before starting another invocation, although that this is a new API to start with so it could be reasonable to define its relationship to promises right from the start. If there's a super common case where this would be undesirable behavior I'd be interested to hear more about it.",
